## Frontend Errors

### Error: "Failed to save recipe. Please try again."
**Symptoms:**
- Save button doesn't work
- Recipe saving fails silently
- User sees generic error message

**Root Cause:**
Multiple possible causes - authentication, database, or API issues

**Solution:**
```javascript
// Enhanced error handling for recipe saving
const saveRecipe = async (recipe) => {
  try {
    // Check authentication first
    if (!window.authManager || !window.authManager.isLoggedIn()) {
      throw new Error('Please log in to save recipes');
    }

    // Validate recipe data
    if (!recipe || !recipe.title) {
      throw new Error('Invalid recipe data');
    }

    // Make API call with proper error handling
    const response = await fetch('/api/saved-recipes/save', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        ...window.authManager.getAuthHeaders()
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({ recipe })
    });

    if (!response.ok) {
      const errorData = await response.json();
      throw new Error(errorData.error || 'Failed to save recipe');
    }

    const result = await response.json();
    showSuccess('Recipe saved successfully!');
    return result;

  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Save recipe error:', error);
    showError(error.message || 'Failed to save recipe. Please try again.');
    throw error;
  }
};
```

**Prevention:**
- Implement comprehensive error handling
- Validate data before API calls
- Provide specific error messages
- Test all error scenarios

### Error: "Generated recipes are not shown"
**Symptoms:**
- Recipes generate but don't display
- Page shows loading state indefinitely
- User sees empty results

**Root Cause:**
Recipe persistence issue - recipes not saved to localStorage

**Solution:**
```javascript
// Implement recipe persistence
const saveRecipesToStorage = (recipes) => {
  try {
    localStorage.setItem('recipe_finder_recipes', JSON.stringify(recipes));
    console.log('💾 Saved recipes to storage:', recipes.length, 'recipes');
  } catch (error) {
    console.warn('Failed to save recipes to localStorage:', error);
  }
};

const loadRecipesFromStorage = () => {
  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem('recipe_finder_recipes');
    if (saved) {
      const recipes = JSON.parse(saved);
      console.log('📦 Loaded recipes from storage:', recipes.length, 'recipes');
      return recipes;
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.warn('Failed to load recipes from localStorage:', error);
  }
  return [];
};

// Load recipes on page initialization
const initializeApp = () => {
  this.loadIngredientsFromStorage();
  this.loadRecipesFromStorage();
  this.bindEvents();
  this.updateUI();
  this.displayRecipes(this.currentRecipes);
};
```

**Prevention:**
- Always implement data persistence
- Load saved data on page initialization
- Handle localStorage errors gracefully

## Performance Errors

### Error: "Page loads slowly"
**Symptoms:**
- Long loading times
- Unresponsive UI
- Poor user experience

**Root Cause:**
Multiple factors - large bundle size, slow API calls, inefficient rendering

**Solution:**
```javascript
// Implement lazy loading for images
const lazyLoadImages = () => {
  const images = document.querySelectorAll('img[data-src]');
  const imageObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        const img = entry.target;
        img.src = img.dataset.src;
        img.removeAttribute('data-src');
        imageObserver.unobserve(img);
      }
    });
  });

  images.forEach(img => imageObserver.observe(img));
};

// Implement debounced search
const debounce = (func, wait) => {
  let timeout;
  return function executedFunction(...args) {
    const later = () => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      func(...args);
    };
    clearTimeout(timeout);
    timeout = setTimeout(later, wait);
  };
};
```

**Prevention:**
- Optimize bundle size
- Implement lazy loading
- Use efficient algorithms
- Monitor performance metrics

## Network Errors

### Error: "Network request failed"
**Symptoms:**
- API calls fail
- Users see network error messages
- Offline functionality doesn't work

**Root Cause:**
Network connectivity issues or server unavailability

**Solution:**
```javascript
// Implement retry logic with exponential backoff
const retryWithBackoff = async (fn, maxRetries = 3) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (error) {
      if (i === maxRetries - 1) throw error;
      
      const delay = Math.pow(2, i) * 1000; // Exponential backoff
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
    }
  }
};

// Enhanced fetch with retry
const fetchWithRetry = async (url, options = {}) => {
  return retryWithBackoff(async () => {
    const response = await fetch(url, options);
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}`);
    }
    return response;
  });
};
```

**Prevention:**
- Implement retry logic
- Provide offline functionality
- Handle network errors gracefully
- Monitor network status

